From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sun4i: a523: bootstrap first DE AHB load

The A523 TG5050 TCON currently produces no vblank interrupt until the DE
has a valid first datapath configuration. The DE integration deferred every
AHB shadow load to the TCON vblank callback, which creates a bootstrap
cycle: no DE load means no scanout, and no scanout means no callback.

Perform one synchronous AHB load after the first atomic plane commit. This
is limited to the initial non-RCQ load; subsequent commits retain the
vblank-gated path needed to avoid tearing. The call runs while the existing
DE arm lock is held, as required by sun55i_de_do_arm().

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -344,4 +344,5 @@
 static enum hrtimer_restart sun55i_de_arm_timer(struct hrtimer *t);
 static u32 sun55i_de_arm_target(struct sun55i_de *de);
+static void sun55i_de_do_arm(struct sun55i_de *de);
 
 static struct sun55i_de_block *de_blk(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer, unsigned int i)
@@ -1069,5 +1069,7 @@
 	de->commit_seq++;
 	dbg_commits++;
 	de->arm_pending = true;
+	if (!de->armed_once && !use_rcq && de->mmio)
+		sun55i_de_do_arm(de);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&de->arm_lock, flags);
 }
